==Strategy==
The very first Advent stage in The Battle Cats and once the hardest stage in the game, No Plan A can still run over the unprepared. With a devastating sniper boss and aggressive Angel pushers, your standard plan of stacking up ranged attackers goes out of the window.

The boss, Cruel Angel Clionel has much higher stats than most enemies you may have encountered so far. She packs a titanic 2,400,000 HP, and stands at an absurd 600 range. But thanks to [[Long Distance]], Clionel can pierce up to 1200 range. Combine this with constant attacks that do 32,000 damage, enough to one- or two-shot most cats and a 30% chance to Slow. Luckily for you, Long Distance also means Clionel has a blindspot of 400, allowing rushers to easily sneak in and attack without facing retaliation.

Cruel Angel Clionel also comes with support. The Trolly Bloggers that spawn constantly may die to a light breeze, but their constant Knockbacks can disrupt meatshield flow and cause you to mistime attackers. The main support, however, are the Angelic Sleipnirs. They have good HP, cover Clionel's blindspot almost perfectly and have constant attacks with a chance to Knockback that cause the same manner of issues as Trolly Bloggers'. This stage alternates between these Sleipnirs, and Angelic Gories. Each Angelic Gory is buffed to a magnification of 200%, giving them almost 200K HP and over 20K DPS! Considering the fact that they spawn in groups later in the fight, these Gories are a massive threat, though they are also your main source of cash.

With No Plan A, you'll have to resort to Plan B, aka Plan [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]]. While over a decade old, Plan B is still the most effective strategy to this day.

#Firstly, spawn a rusher, preferably [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] for its Double Bounty, to gather cash from the Trolly Bloggers and stall Clionel.
#Lure Sleipnir and Clionel to the Cat Base so that Sleipnir gets ahead of Clionel by a good margin.
#Deploy Awakened Bahamut Cat on the Angelic Gory to dispatch it. Then spam all your rushers clear a path to Sleipnir, letting Bahamut chain him to a stagger before Clionel finishes her attack.
#Use the Cat Cannon to interrupt Clionel's attack.

At this point, Bahamut will hopefully force his way into Clionel's blind spot and deal the finishing blow to Angelic Sleipnir. If your rushers are strong enough, you can actually defeat Clionel in this initial rush, however, the second Sleipnir sometimes arrives just in time to rescue Clionel. If such happens, just last until Bahamut goes off cooldown and perform the chain again.

Even then, this strategy has caveats. For one, Sleipnir knocking back your units at the wrong time could screw you over, meaning you can simply lose from bad luck. Secondly, Sleipnir's position relative to Clionel must be in a sweetspot. If Sleipnir is too far in front of Clionel, your units won't be able to infiltrate her blindspot during the Bahamut chain and will get destroyed. If Sleipnir is not far enough, he'll be knocked back behind Clionel and will be able to survive, ruining your run. To remedy this, if Sleipnir turns out to be too close, spawn a rusher during to bait out an attack from Clionel. If Sleipnir happens to be too far, spawn a weaker rusher to bait a few attacks from Sleipnir instead.

If you find yourself being pushed to your base by the Angelic Gories, try an alternative strategy: After your rusher kills off the first few Trolly Bloggers and Sleipnir spawns, start sending in waves of meat shields and Ramen Cat to help gain ground, rather than fighting close to your base. Though this gives you a much larger window to defeat the Angelic Gories, it also makes rushers harder to time into Clionel's blindspot. Thus, if fighting far from the Cat Base, try spawning rushers when Clionel's attack animation starts—this usually results in Clionel's attack missing said rushers and hitting right in front of them instead.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Bahamut, being a fast rusher with massive DPS at the cost of range and health, is the essence of many strategies as he'll be their main damage source, whether against Clionel or the peons.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist/Ramen Cat]] - Since most enemies here are Angels, Artist's singular knockback, high health and resistance against them make him more than ideal for this particular showdown. If you have his True Form, even better. At level 50 with True Form and maxed Talents (besides Resist Curse),  he turns it into a cakewalk, only needing some support to help push against the enemies, useful to know for Abyssal clears.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Delivery Cat]]: A cheap rusher with good damage against Angels. His True Form, Cafeteria Cat, is such an improvement that you can win just by spamming level 50 Cafeteria Cats with Research Combos, but he can still help even in Evolved Form.
*[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]]/[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] - As supplementary rushers, Crazed Giraffe and Maglev can both take advantage of their extreme speed to pin Clionel and inflict extra damage. Maglev even backs this up with the Extra Money ability, which, combined with its full backswing and knockback effects from Trolly Blogger/Sleipnir can either do serious damage or provide a boost to your economy.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] - Cleanerbot's impressive health for its low cost, high speed, singular knockback and immunity to Knockback/Slow greatly aids rush strategies. It can stall Sleipnir, Clionel and Trolly Blogger while buying rushers much more time to inflict damage, though it does have a long recharge time. It's recommended to use its True Form, which is even faster and tankier, but you may end up struggling with [[March to Death (Merciless)|March to Death]] more than No Plan A, so you'll have to balance your priorities.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - Can Can Cat is a powerful single-target attacker with huge damage at close range. Primarily useful against Angelic Gories, with Extra Money and Move Speed Up Talents allowing it to get even more value for its low cost.
*[[A Gift of Cats (Rare Cat)|A Gift of Cats]] - Very fast rusher that can freeze angels for a few seconds. At level 30, they can also hit Slepnir and freeze it. This can allow slower units to infiltrate the blindspot
*[[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]] - With Speed Talents, Juliet becomes a better version of A Gift of Cats here, having a full second longer Freeze and a 10% higher chance of Freeze activation.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Fishman is a fast all-purpose rusher that can be effective in infiltrating Clionel's blindspot.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Courier Cat's high stats makes him a very strong rusher for this stage.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Kalisa]]: Kalisa is a fast rusher with massive damage to Angels and full backswing attacks. She can fit inside Cruel Angel Clionel's blind spot and nuke the Angelic Gories in no time flat. She is thus ideal for accompanying Bahamut in the chain. Be aware that Sleipnir can either knock her back into Clionel's effective range or stunlock her to death.
*[[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|Guardian Gamereon]] or [[Thunder God Zeus (Uber Rare Cat)|The Majestic Zeus]]: Both can tank an ungodly amount of punishment and can help clear out the Angelic Gories and Trolly Bloggers. They can help give you breathing room and even dish out some damage on their own, but be careful of knockbacks from the Sleipnir and Bloggers.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]: Fast, spammable and deals massive damage to Angels. He can easily keep the Angelic Gories at bay and shoot down Clionel if he makes into her blind spot.
*[[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Ushiwakamaru]] - The zenith of Angelic destruction, Ushiwakamaru's main highlights include his Resistance/Insane Damage ability against Angels. Both forms can be used here to great effect, but they aren't perfect - his first form can solo the stage only with Research Combos, and the latter requires considerable support to actually get a hit on, as it isn't immune to Weaken/Slow.
*[[Sarukani (Uber Rare Cat)|The One-Hit Wonders]] - High range and Strong Against Angels, with immunity to slow and weaken. Ideal for taking on any enemy, though Sleipnir's knockback may pester them.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Yukimura]] - Yukimura can act as a second Awakened Bahamut and assist with rushing down Sleipnir and Clionel. In Abyssal clears, with boosted levels and talents unlocked, he could basically substitute for Bahamut.
*[[Juvens (Uber Rare Cat)|Juvens]] - Excellent health and resistance to Angels combined with dodge allows him to stand his ground, even dodging Sleipnir's pushing attacks often. Offers top-level protection while delivering massive DPS and having a quick enough recharge to keep up if he is destroyed.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]] - Excellent health, is fast enough to enter Clionel's blindspot, can stunlock her with knockback and hold his own against her for a decent while, and is cheap and has quite the fast recharge.
*[[Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sonic]] - Deals Massive Damage to Angels, and has extremely fast speed, making him easy to use and very rewarding.
*[[Iz the Dancer (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Alluring Dancer]] - Just like in other advent stages, her ability to tank and deal ridiculous damage helps a lot in this stage.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]] - Fairly cheap, tanky, great damage and able to [[Weaken]] the Angels here. Her Weaken pairs extremely well with Awakened Bahamut Cat, as he will be able to take more hits from Angelic Sleipnir and even survive an attack from Clionel. Artist Cat benefits too, as Lunacia's pierce and Explosions will keep the Trolly Bloggers at bay.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Landshaker Kozuchimaru]] - A very solid unit for this stage, with massive damage against Angels, being fully capable of taking down both Clionel and the rest of its supports. His high speed makes it easier to reach the boss's blind spot, and, if that weren't enough, it can take advantage of knockbacks from Trolly Bloggers and Slepnirs to land multiple hits in a very short time.
*[[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Li’l Valkyrie]] - Surprisingly, if she is directly attacking Clionel, Li’l Valkyrie stands perfectly out of Sleipnir’s range while still being inside Clionel’s blindspot, allowing her to do lots of damage to Clionel, although you'll need good timing and must be wary of the Angelic Gories or Sleipnir getting in her way.

