==Abyssal Strategy==
The following lineups are designed to work on their own; however, it is recommended and encouraged to add to them as you see fit. Certain [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] can dramatically simplify the stage, so don't be afraid to include them alongside these strategies.

{{Lineup
|Manic Lion Cat|50
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|40
|talent2 = Explosion Lv. 10
|name = Lineup 1
}}

'''Difficulty:''' ★☆☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' Send out Manic Lion Cat to clear the way for Awakened Bahamut Cat, then simply time him so that he's not hit by Clionel. Keep spamming Manic Lions and the stage is as good as beaten (so long as you're not unlucky with Angelic Sleipnir's Knockback).

{{Lineup
|Doctor Cat
|Manic Island Cat
|Island Cat
|Ramen Cat|50
|talent4 = Knockback Resist Lv. 10, Defense Buff Lv. 10
|Courier Cat|50
|name = Lineup 2
}}

'''Difficulty:''' ☆☆☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' Spam Courier, Ramen, and Manic Island Cat. Ramen tanks the Angels well, so even without Research Combos he'll still stop the nasty Angels dead in their tracks. Courier is there to kill off Trolly Bloggers, as Ramen struggles to withstand their Knockback ability. If you're lucky, they'll rush down Clionel and kill her almost instantly.

{{Lineup
|Manic Eraser Cat|50
|Green Shell Cat|50
|Bullet Train Cat|50
|Fiend Cat|50
|talent4 = Target Angel, Tough Vs
|name = Lineup 3
|notes = Fiend Cat's Resist Talent is not required, though highly recommended for ensuring he makes it into Clionel's blindspot.
}}

'''Difficulty:''' ★★☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' Summon Bullet Train as soon as Clionel spawns, and immediately follow that up with Green Shell to prevent the Trolly Bloggers from pushing via Knockback. Start sending out Fiend Cats to force Clionel back to the enemy base. With some luck, Angelic Sleipnir will be pushed behind everything else and won't be capable of posing even the slightest threat to your Fiend Cats, who will be continuously chipping away at the enemy base. The Gories may prove to be a slight nuisance, but a good line of meatshields will render them a non-issue for the most part.

{{Lineup
|Li'l King Dragon Cat
|Jiangshi Cat
|Wrestling Cat
|Fishman Cat|50
|Eraser Cat|20+60
|Jelly Dumpling Cat|50
|Manic Macho Legs|50
|Mushroom Cat|50
|Can Can Cat|50
|talent9 = Move Speed Up Lv. 10
|name = Lineup 4
|cannon = Thunderbolt
|items = Rich Cat
}}

'''Difficulty:''' ★★★★☆

'''Battle:''' The aim of the game is to brute force your way into Clionel's blind spot. Jelly Dumpling, Can Can, and Fishman Cat will be doing most of the heavy lifting in terms of damage, as they will be your primary method of damaging the Angelic Sleipnirs. This strategy hinges a lot on Sleipnir Knockback RNG, which can and will brick runs if two manage to stack up. Thankfully, they're not very bulky here, so all it takes is a few direct hits from the aforementioned cats to send them packing. Mushroom Cat is useful to stop the Angelic Gories in their tracks, since multiple stacked up tend to be a death sentence.

{{Lineup
|Necro-Dancer Cat
|Skelecat
|Hyper Mr.
|Cafeteria Cat|50
|Riceball Cat|50
|talent5 = Defense Buff Lv. 10
|name = Lineup 5
}}

'''Difficulty:''' ★★☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' Spam Cafeteria Cats the moment the stage starts and you have enough money, then start spamming Riceball Cats too. Your goal is to sneak as many Cafeterias and Riceballs into Clionels blindspot as humanly possible; with good timing you should be able to swarm Clionel at the enemy base and instantly eliminate her before the second Sleipnir even has a chance to spawn. The Riceballs will be able to prevent the Trolly Bloggers from messing you up, for the most part at least.

