==Trivia==
*Prior to April 2017 (February 2018 in the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]]), this stage had no known schedule.
*No Plan A's Japanese name, Neko Hokan Keikaku (ネコ補完計画, "Cat Complementary Project"), is a reference to the Japanese name of ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Human_Instrumentality_Project Human Instrumentality Project], Jinrui Hokan Keikaku (人類補完計画, "Human Complementary Project").
*Unlike the other Deadly [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stages]], No Plan A's [[Stage Difficulties|star difficulty]] is only ★8, not ★9. This may be because it is the only Advent to have been added before [[Version 5.0 Update|Version 5.0]], meaning it was designed without power creep from [[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha cats]]' [[True Form]]s, [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed Cats]]' True Forms and [[Catseye]]s in mind.
*In both the mobile version and [[The Battle Cats Unite!|Nintendo Switch]] version of the game, Clionel Ascendant was the first Advent Stage to be released.
**Clionel Ascendant was made available in the Nintendo Switch version via the [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.7 Update#September 15, 2023 Update Patch|September 15, 2023 Update Patch]].

